questions.text:
You are going to spend a week in London. You are planning to travel on a tiny budget and don’t have many connections in Britain. Your English pen-friend has agreed to meet you at the airport and help with getting around London. Write a letter to your pen-friend in which you
 give the details of your arrival in Britain;
 say what you look like to be recognized;
 explain what you would like to do and see in London.
 Write a letter of at least 100 words. Do not use your real name or any personal information.
 Start your letter in an appropriate way.
